---
import NoteHandwritten from "@/components/content/NoteHandwritten.astro";
import Section from "@/components/wrapper/Section.astro";
import Heading from "@/components/typography/Heading.astro";
import Eyebrow from "@/components/typography/Eyebrow.astro";
import ContentWrapper from "@/components/wrapper/ContentWrapper.astro";
import Paragraph from "@/components/typography/Paragraph.astro";

const sectionLabelClass =
  "background-yellow angled-text-right-1 emphasis font-figtree padding-inline-2 padding-block-3 margin-top-3 text-wrap-nowrap";

---

<Section id="about" fullHeight={true}>
    <ContentWrapper>

      <Heading tag="h2" class="radius-small background-yellow angled-text-right-2 emphasis font-quicksand padding-inline-2 padding-block-2 margin-top-3 text-wrap-nowrap drop-shadow-text">
        a little about me
      </Heading>
    </ContentWrapper>
    <ContentWrapper variant="columns">
        
    <NoteHandwritten slot="column2" text="The person designing it is the person building it." />
   
    <Paragraph variant="body" maxWidth={70} class="h3">
      I’m Sean. I design and build digital products — from high traffic, content-driven websites and high performance web
      applications to native, local-first software built with Rust and Erlang. 
    </Paragraph>
    
<Paragraph variant="body" maxWidth={70}>      My work connects the visual details with the code behind them: how content
      reads, how an interaction feels and how easily a product can grow. I enjoy
      moving between design and development, working through an idea until it
      feels right and works well in someone’s hands.
    </Paragraph>
<Paragraph variant="body" maxWidth={70}>       I come from a background of software engineering, but I also
      care deeply about the details that make a product feel polished and intuitive, which has led me to my current role as a design engineer. My work features the rigor of traditional software engineering practices with the benefit of a design-first approach. I never hand off a design to a separate team; I build it myself. This often comes with longer lead times, but leads to more cohesive, polished products that are easy to maintain and evolve.
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph variant="body" maxWidth={60}>
      Whether I’m working on the web or native applications, I care about software that is clear to
      use and understandable to the people maintaining it. I can help shape an
      early idea, carry a design through development or join your team where you
      need an extra pair of hands.
    </Paragraph>
    </ContentWrapper>
  </Section>

  <style>
